## Methods
Synthesis and characterization of MOF-907. $\mathrm{\bfH}_{3}\mathrm{\bfBTB}$ $(0.012\mathrm{g},0.027\mathrm{mmol})$ and $\mathrm{\DeltaH_{2}N D C}$ $(0.01\mathrm{g},0.046\mathrm{mmol})$ were dissolved in $3\mathrm{mL}$ DMF. A mixture of $1\mathrm{mL}$ DMF and acetic acid $(0.20\mathrm{mL}$ , $3.49\mathrm{mmol}$ ) containing iron(III) nitrate nonahydrate $(0.02\mathrm{g},0.050\mathrm{mmol})$ was then added to the solution containing $\mathrm{H}_{3}\mathrm{BTB}$ and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{NDC}$ . The reacted solution was subsequently placed in a glass $\mathrm{8\mL}$ vial and heated at $120^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $24\mathrm{h}$ . After that time elapsed, orange cube-shaped crystals were then collected by decantation.
Single crystal X-ray diffraction studies. Data was collected at beamline 11.3.1 at the Advanced Light Source, Lawrence Berkeley National Lab at $0.77490\mathrm{\AA}$ A single crystal of MOF-907 was isolated from the mother liquor of the reaction, mounted on a MiTeGen® kapton loop and placed in a 100(2) K nitrogen cold stream.
Polymerization of methyl methacrylate. A $3.0\mathrm{mg}$ of activated MOF-907 (0.0032 mmol) was loaded into a $10\mathrm{mL}$ glass vial for use in the microwave system. $1.0\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF $\cdot13\mathrm{mmol}$ ), $301\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of methyl methacrylate (MMA, $2.81\mathrm{mmol}$ ), and $1.9\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of ethyl $\alpha$ -bromoisobutyrate (EBiB, $1.29\times10^{-5}\mathrm{mmol},$ ) or $2.3\upmu\mathrm{L}$ ethyl $\alpha$ -bromophenylacetate (EBPA, $\dot{1.29}\times10^{-5}\mathrm{mmol}$ ) were then added into the vial. The vial was sealed with a microwave cap. The reaction system was stirred for $30\mathrm{min}$ at room temperature (covered with Al foil to prevent light interference) before loading into the microwave system. The synthesis condition for the polymerization reaction was set up at $100^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and $30\mathrm{min}$ with $200\mathrm{W}$ of power under a closed system. When the reaction was completed, MOF-907 was collected by centrifugation and washed with dicholoromethane 3–5 times. The polyMMA product was crystallized in a solution of $30~\mathrm{mL}$ MeOH and washed with methanol 3 times. The polymer was dried at room temperature for 2 days or under vacuum for $^{2\mathrm{h}}$ . The following conditions were optimized: amount of initiator, different
concentration of the reaction, temperature, power, and the reaction time. The reported conditions above are optimized. The same procedure was applied using other catalysts (HKUST-1, Ni-VNU-74(II), and ${\mathrm{FeCl}}_{3}^{\cdot},$ ).
Crystallographic data for MOF-907 was deposited in the CCDC. The deposition number is 1547518. This data can be obtained free of charge from the Cambridge Crystallographic Data Centre via www.ccdc.cam.ac.uk/data_request/cif. All other data that support the findings in this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.
